# Design Language

## Tone

Premium, elegant, emotional, cinematic, modern, lightweight, warm. Avoid cluttered UI, corporate SaaS dashboards, aggressive gradients, excessive glassmorphism.

## Mobile-First

Design small screens first; thumb-friendly; smooth scroll; low-end Android support. Desktop adapts from mobile.

## Typography

**Headings (serif):** Playfair Display, Cormorant Garamond, DM Serif Display  
**Body (sans):** Inter, Poppins, Manrope  
Max 2 font families. Headings: large, breathable, high line-height. Body: readable, minimal. No tiny sizes or decorative body fonts.

## Spacing Scale

Use consistently: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64. Generous whitespace; avoid cramped layouts.

## Color

Luxurious, warm, romantic: ivory, champagne, gold, rose, beige, warm neutrals. One primary accent + neutral background system. Dark mode: cinematic, not cyberpunk. No neon or noisy gradients.

## Buttons & Cards

- Buttons: soft, premium, medium radius, subtle hover (desktop), clean padding
- Cards: lightweight, soft shadows, subtle borders, generous spacing

## Forms

Clear labels, large touch targets, clean focus states. No tiny controls or multi-column mobile forms.

## Dashboard

Calm, focused, lightweight — not admin-panel aesthetics. Editor: left controls, right live preview when layout allows.

## Public Invitations

Cinematic storytelling via typography and hierarchy; avoid animation overload and laggy transitions.

## Motion (UI)

150–500ms; natural easing; fade, gentle slide, subtle scale. Performance over complexity.

## Images & Icons

Emotional, optimized, lazy-loaded, consistent aspect ratios. **Lucide** icons; thin outline; never dominate UI.

## Loading & Empty States

Skeleton loaders, subtle shimmer — no blank screens or aggressive spinners. Empty states: friendly and guiding.

## Accessibility

Readable contrast, scalable type, accessible touch targets (min 44×44px).

## Inspiration

Luxury wedding brands, editorial layouts, premium mobile apps — not enterprise dashboards or crypto landing pages.
